{#
    One record of one entity, as a form.

    THE FIELDS ARRIVE READY TO RENDER. `FormController::controls()` has already decided which
    control each field gets, whether it is editable at all, what its value prints as and whether
    a checkbox is ticked — for the same reason the list formats its cells in PHP: a `datetime`
    comes out of `toValueObject()` as an array, and a wrong type here is a runtime error on the
    page nobody tested with that field.

    `control` IS THE SWITCH, and its values are HTML controls, not ADR 0013's widget keys. The
    mapping between the two is in `FormController::CONTROLS`, which is the single place story
    002-007 replaces when it builds a real element for each of the 21 field types. Until then
    `display` is the honest answer for a relation, a file or a permission matrix: the value is
    shown and not offered, so nothing can be saved that this package cannot yet form.

    THE TABS COME FROM THE `tab` ATTRIBUTE (002-006-0003, ADR 0015), already grouped. One group
    renders without a bar, which is what every entity that states no tab looks like.

    SWITCHING IS CLIENT-SIDE, AND THAT IS NOT A PREFERENCE. Sorting and paging in the list are
    plain links because their state belongs in the URL; a tab must not be, because the form
    holds unsaved input and a server round trip would throw it away. The Stimulus controller is
    declared by the controller only when there is more than one group.

    IT ALSO HAS TO WORK WITHOUT THE CONTROLLER. Every panel is visible until the controller
    hides the inactive ones on connect — the opposite order would leave a form with one
    reachable group if the module failed to load, and a form that silently shows two thirds of
    its fields is worse than one with no tabs at all. For the same reason the buttons are
    `type="button"`: inside a form a bare button submits it.

    NO ADDRESS IS BUILT HERE. `action`, `listUrl` and the prefix behind them come from the
    controller, as in the list view.

    THE TOKEN FIELD IS NOT OPTIONAL. `FormController::save()` verifies it before it speaks to
    the core at all, so a form rendered without it cannot be saved. It is a hidden field plus a
    cookie — `Auth\FormToken` — and the promise ADR 0010 assigned to this story.

    A FINDING GOES TO ITS FIELD WHEN ITS FIELD IS KNOWN, otherwise above the form — the decision
    is `FormController::reject()`'s, the two places are here. The core names no field (gap L19),
    so the one that is known was guessed from the message text at the single place ADR 0014
    allows; when the guess misses, the message is still shown. It never disappears.

    IT SAYS THAT IT IS ONE FINDING, NOT ALL OF THEM. The core fills `errors` with exactly one
    entry (gap L20), so a form with twelve fields needs one save per problem. Saying so is the
    difference between an editor who saves again and one who believes everything else passed.

    A FIELD ERROR IS TIED TO ITS CONTROL with `aria-describedby` and `aria-invalid`, so a screen
    reader reads the message as part of the field rather than as loose text nearby.
#}{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% macro field(field) %}
{% set described = field.error ? 'error-' ~ field.property : '' %}
        <div class="admin-form__field{% if field.error %} admin-form__field--invalid{% endif %}">
{% if field.control == 'checkbox' %}
            <label class="admin-form__label admin-form__label--inline" for="field-{{ field.property }}">
                <input class="admin-form__checkbox" type="checkbox" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}" value="1"{% if field.checked %} checked{% endif %}{% if field.error %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
                {{ field.label }}
            </label>
{% else %}
            <label class="admin-form__label" for="field-{{ field.property }}">{{ field.label }}{% if field.required %} <span class="admin-form__required" aria-hidden="true">*</span>{% endif %}</label>

{% if field.control == 'display' %}
            <p class="admin-form__display" id="field-{{ field.property }}">{{ field.value ?: '—' }}</p>
{% elseif field.control == 'textarea' %}
            <textarea class="admin-form__control" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}" rows="6"{% if field.required %} required{% endif %}{% if field.error %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>{{ field.value }}</textarea>
{% elseif field.control == 'select' %}
            <select class="admin-form__control" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}"{% if field.required %} required{% endif %}{% if field.error %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
{% if not field.required %}
                <option value=""></option>
{% endif %}
{% for option in field.options %}
                <option value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value == field.value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ option.label }}</option>
{% endfor %}
            </select>
{% else %}
            <input class="admin-form__control" type="{{ field.control }}" id="field-{{ field.property }}" name="{{ field.property }}" value="{{ field.value }}"{% if field.maxlength %} maxlength="{{ field.maxlength }}"{% endif %}{% if field.required %} required{% endif %}{% if field.error %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ described }}"{% endif %}>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if field.error %}
            <p class="admin-form__field-error" id="{{ described }}">{{ field.error }}</p>
{% endif %}
        </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% block bodyAttributes %} class="admin"{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
{% import _self as form %}
<main class="admin__main">
    <h1>{{ entity }}{% if isNew %} — neuer Datensatz{% endif %}</h1>

    <p class="admin-form__back"><a href="{{ listUrl }}">Zurück zur Liste</a></p>

{% if error %}
    <p class="admin-form__error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if partial %}
    <p class="admin-form__hint">Das Grundsystem meldet immer nur einen Punkt auf einmal — nach dem Beheben kann beim nächsten Speichern ein weiterer dazukommen.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if tabs is empty %}
    <p class="admin__hint">Diese Entität hat keine bearbeitbaren Felder.</p>
{% else %}
    <form class="admin-form" method="post" action="{{ action }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ tokenField }}" value="{{ token }}">
{% if tabs|length > 1 %}
        <div class="admin-form__tabs" data-controller="admin-tabs">
            <div class="admin-form__tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Feldgruppen">
{% for tab in tabs %}
                <button class="admin-form__tab{% if tab.hasError %} admin-form__tab--invalid{% endif %}" type="button" role="tab" id="tab-{{ tab.index }}" aria-controls="panel-{{ tab.index }}" aria-selected="{{ loop.first ? 'true' : 'false' }}" data-admin-tabs-target="tab" data-action="click->admin-tabs#select keydown->admin-tabs#key">{{ tab.name }}</button>
{% endfor %}
            </div>
{% for tab in tabs %}
            <section class="admin-form__panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-{{ tab.index }}" aria-labelledby="tab-{{ tab.index }}" data-admin-tabs-target="panel"{% if tab.hasError %} data-admin-tabs-invalid="true"{% endif %}>
{% for field in tab.fields %}
{{ form.field(field) }}
{% endfor %}
            </section>
{% endfor %}
        </div>
{% else %}
{% for field in tabs[0].fields %}
{{ form.field(field) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

        <div class="admin-form__actions">
            <button class="admin-form__submit" type="submit">{% if isNew %}Anlegen{% else %}Speichern{% endif %}</button>
        </div>
    </form>
{% endif %}
</main>
{% endblock %}
